9,15,3,1172,979,400,87,59,258,10293,59,258,36958,11,481,17,10699,36665,7,18,26266,258,36958,15087,30,151645,198,151644,77091,198],"messages":[{"content":"Solve the problem step by step. Give your final answer in \\boxed{...}.\n\nWhat is the value of $b+c$ if $x^2+bx+c>0$ only when $x\\in (-\\infty, -2)\\cup(3,\\infty)$?","role":"user"}],"rendered_sha256":"77517261fd0b9b03e54658579a2006d155e1306599852743ec97c1e712eb44d3"},"seconds":7.199702262878418,"seed":852665307586774365,"stop":"eos","text":"To solve the problem, we need to determine the values of \\(b\\) and \\(c\\) such that the quadratic inequality \\(x^2 + bx + c > 0\\) holds only when \\(x \\in (-\\infty, -2) \\cup (3, \\infty)\\). This means the quadratic expression \\(x^2 + bx + c\\) is positive outside the interval \\([-2, 3]\\) and zero at \\(x = -2\\) and \\(x = 3\\).\n\nGiven that the quadratic expression is zero at \\(x = -2\\) and \\(x = 3\\), we can express the quadratic polynomial in its factored form:\n\\[x^2 + bx + c = (x + 2)(x - 3).\\]\n\nNext, we expand the factored form to find the coefficients \\(b\\) and \\(c\\):\n\\[\n(x + 2)(x - 3) = x^2 - 3x + 2x - 6 = x^2 - x - 6.\n\\]\nFrom this, we can see that \\(b = -1\\) and \\(c = -6\\).\n\nWe are asked to find the value of \\(b + c\\):\n\\[\nb + c = -1 + (-6) = -7.\n\\]\n\nThus, the value of \\(b + c\\) is \\(\\boxed{-7}\\)."},"grade":{"answer":"\\boxed{-7}","correct":true,"format":"boxed","parseable":true},"id":"algebra:732"}
